  "journal_check_basis": "The native journal issue manifest (METS) counts document types. MODS supplies authors, original and translated titles, explicit summary fields and the online publication date. Exact DOI queries independently confirm the journal identifiers in Crossref. Its records for these two issues give only 2026, so date-range queries alone miss both issues.",
  "source_limits": [
    "Arts and Humanities, two journals from the same publisher, supplied 48/100 and 40/62 works respectively in the October–November and August cohorts. Authored research books reached the input in both periods.",
    "Of 20 Portuguese-original books in the broader October–November catalogue, 15 fell outside pilot subject codes, 4 lacked a matched original date and identity, and one lacked a usable title, abstract or credited author/editor pair. None reached the input. All accepted descriptions or abstracts in both cohorts carried English metadata, including translations of French research.",
    "The three OpenEdition presses produced no eligible new whole books in these windows. Chapters, reviews, editorial introductions and backlist digitizations are counted in the source decisions.",
    "Two transient registry checks initially left a Portuguese title and an August book unresolved. Targeted later checks excluded the former and confirmed the latter. A partial source is flagged in a dated pilot.",
    "The two four-week windows sample different seasons and source releases. The recorded article and book volumes do not establish comprehensive field coverage."
  ],
